{
  "id": "a2-rational-04",
  "version": 2,
  "title": "Geometric sequences",
  "xp": 15,
  "tags": [
    "algebra",
    "sequences"
  ],
  "learn": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Multiplying by the same amount",
      "body": "In a geometric sequence each term is the previous one times a fixed number, the common ratio $r$. For $3,6,12,24,\\ldots$ the ratio is $r=2$. The $n$th term is $a_n=a_1\\cdot r^{n-1}$. This is an exponential function of $n$."
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "example",
      "title": "The sequence $3,6,12,\\ldots$",
      "body": "Here $a_1=3$ and $r=2$.",
      "steps": [
        "Term 8: $a_8=3\\cdot 2^7=384$",
        "Which term is 96? $3\\cdot 2^{n-1}=96$",
        "$2^{n-1}=32=2^5$, so $n-1=5$",
        "$n=6$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "example",
      "title": "A shrinking sequence $81,27,9,\\ldots$",
      "body": "Divide a term by the one before to find $r$.",
      "steps": [
        "$r=\\frac{27}{81}=\\frac{1}{3}$",
        "$a_6=81\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^5$",
        "$=\\frac{81}{243}=\\frac{1}{3}$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "tip",
      "body": "Arithmetic adds, geometric multiplies. A negative ratio makes the signs alternate: $5,-10,20,-40,\\ldots$ has $r=-2$."
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "Find the common ratio of $3,6,12,24,\\ldots$",
      "accepted": [
        "2"
      ],
      "keypad": "numeric",
      "explanation": "$6\\div 3=2$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "For $3,6,12,\\ldots$ find $a_8$.",
      "accepted": [
